<title>PERU: Peru says first half oil output up, natgas down.</title>
<headline>Peru says first half oil output up, natgas down.</headline>
<dateline>LIMA 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Peru produced an average of 121,698 barrels per day (bpd) of crude oil in the first half, up 2.5 percent from the same period last year, the Energy and Mines Ministry said Thursday.</p>
<p>Natural gas output between January and June averaged 20.44 million cubic feet per day, down 1.5 percent from the first half last year, the ministry added in a monthly report.</p>
<p>((-- Andrew Cawthorne, Lima newsroom, 511 221-2134))</p>
